WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.640
Chris Gore, Founder/Owner of&nbsp;
FilmThreat/Author/Filmmaker: Do I want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.800
see the sequel to A Christmas Story starring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.240
Peter Billingsley as a grown-up version&nbsp;
of himself, maybe if it's set in the 60’s?

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.160
Film Courage:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.800
Chris, without checking your phone can you name&nbsp;
all of the Christmas films you can think of?

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.880
Chris: Oh wow! Well, there's a lot, there's&nbsp;
so many that I love. It's A Wonderful Life,

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.720
 A Christmas Story, Bad Santa.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.440
I mean I don't know if you consider The Grinch&nbsp;
That Stole Christmas it's not a Christmas movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.720
per se but I always associate that with Christmas&nbsp;
along with the Peanuts Christmas special.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.360
I mean Oh goodness there's a bunch&nbsp;
those are just like off the top of my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.280
head. My personal favorites, the ones&nbsp;
that I make sure to watch every year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.680
and then there's ones that people would argue&nbsp;
aren't necessarily Christmas movies like Die Hard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:59.280
But I would put that in that category just&nbsp;
because I love the whole…I think it's become an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:05.280
ugly Christmas sweater that says “Ho, ho, ho, now&nbsp;
I have a gun.” I’ve seen people wear that costume.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.240
Film Courage: So you would consider&nbsp;
Die Hard a Christmas movie?

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.840
Chris: For me it is, for me&nbsp;
Die Hard is a Christmas movie.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.640
Film Courage: What needs to happen in a&nbsp;
Christmas film? Does Christmas need to be saved?

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:25.520
Chris: Yeah, I wonder if you could even make an&nbsp;
earnest Christmas movie now that isn't relegated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:32.320
to the Hallmark Channel? By that I mean a wide&nbsp;
release Christmas movie that goes to theaters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:38.000
that would appeal to people who don't care about&nbsp;
Christmas, it's just a heartwarming movie that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.640
takes place over the holidays. I think that the&nbsp;
thing that needs to happen in a Christmas movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:49.440
1) it's got to take place during Christmas which&nbsp;
Batman Returns by Tim Burton does. It takes place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:59.200
during Christmas, it also somehow the message of&nbsp;
Christmas has to be in there woven in some way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:08.240
a realization a love of fellow (your fellow man)&nbsp;
and I think that has to be a big part of it and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:16.000
lessons have to be learned right? I think that's&nbsp;
part of Christmas is this for me there's a feeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.840
that exists around Christmas that is&nbsp;
palpable and it usually starts around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.720
Christmas eve night that you could just feel&nbsp;
and Christmas is the next day and it's sort of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:39.600
reconfirmation of your relationships&nbsp;
of people close to you and your family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:50.240
or your significant other and a way to reach&nbsp;
out to family and friends and say Hey, I care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:58.400
about you. That has to be a big part of it even if&nbsp;
it's woven in the most simple way. Yes I know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:05.200
It's A Wonderful Life is dated but I feel like&nbsp;
what's sad to me is that certain people would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:12.560
think that the message of It's A wonderful Life&nbsp;
is dated that is where I have concerns because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:22.320
I feel that in particular this comes with acts of&nbsp;
heroism whether it is in an actual superhero movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:30.640
or acts of self-sacrifice or acts of kindness&nbsp;
towards a fellow human for no reason whatsoever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.760
whatsoever other than to do that and I&nbsp;
feel like that as a value has been lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:46.240
and I notice it in modern films and television&nbsp;
I feel like that kindness towards your fellow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:04:02.000
person, human, American, neighbor, it's not as&nbsp;
present as it used to be unfortunately although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.400
I will say if you spent some time on social media&nbsp;
and you get up and walk outside your house and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:13.840
normally that feeling isn't present but Christmas&nbsp;
is. First of all I love those Christmas movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:22.880
but the Peanuts Christmas special would never&nbsp;
be made today in specifically because of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:30.720
quotes from the Bible and there was even&nbsp;
controversy at the time about like is this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:37.360
going to be a religious special and it was and now&nbsp;
it's something that has survived until today but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:47.040
I think it'd be incredibly difficult outside of&nbsp;
a small release religious show film showing at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:53.840
churches and whatnot or something for the Hallmark&nbsp;
channel you wouldn't see those kinds of religious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.840 --> 00:05:01.040
ideals even if it was simply the ideas without&nbsp;
the Bible verses. I don't think you would see that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:11.040
and it's it's again another fracturing of our&nbsp;
audience right? There's a huge audience that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:17.360
would love to see a movie about Christmas even&nbsp;
if it's only peripherally about Christmas. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:27.120
yeah I think it is those values, those&nbsp;
rituals are eroding and they're not as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:33.920
popular on a mass scale as they used to&nbsp;
be. I'm just saying what I have observed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:43.120
but try to get a Christmas special with religious&nbsp;
themes, that doesn't on a mainstream level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:48.560
it'll never happen. Not something made by a major&nbsp;
corporation is not going to do, it's going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:56.640
relocated to what they call a vertical&nbsp;
which is a small audience. So there you are.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:59.800
Film Courage: When would you&nbsp;
typically play a Christmas movie?

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.760
Chris: Well Christmas is&nbsp;
my second favorite holiday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:10.160
My first favorite holiday is Halloween,&nbsp;
the decorations go up in late September,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:18.160
It's a month-long celebration. It's horror movies&nbsp;
for the entire month and so I love Halloween.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:25.360
Christmas I sort of like once I’m&nbsp;
into the turkey around Thanksgiving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:35.600
then the Christmas movies go into rotation.&nbsp;
And then it's like the ones like which actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:41.840
still has some heartfelt messages, Bad Santa you&nbsp;
would not think this and you will never look at a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:49.840
pickle the same way but Bad Santa kind of is&nbsp;
also one of my Christmas holiday favorites.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:53.120
Film Courage: If you were&nbsp;
to write a Christmas film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.329
would you be the protagonist? Would you&nbsp;
see yourself in the protagonist role?

00:06:57.329 --> 00:07:02.800
Chris: Well if I wrote a Christmas movie I&nbsp;
would not be the protagonist of that movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:11.360
But I’d like to see if Hollywood could make a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:18.000
Christmas movie. To me one of my all-time&nbsp;
favorites is a Christmas Story. Now could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:24.560
you make that movie today? Could you make a&nbsp;
movie where a kid (little Ralphie) just wants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:36.240
a gun for Christmas? Today's climate it's&nbsp;
a little different. I would love to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:41.520
and I’ve heard rumors that Peter Billingsley&nbsp;
is going to do an update of A Christmas Story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.320
I’d love to see a sequel to that&nbsp;
movie with his character all grown up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:55.200
maybe he wants a different type of gun for&nbsp;
Christmas, who knows? But that movie is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.200 --> 00:08:07.120
just about Christmas, it's also a reflection of&nbsp;
this bygone era and I just wonder if Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:14.000
is capable of making a movie about Christmas?&nbsp;
I feel (and this is not so much a reflection of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:19.840
the industry) I think audiences would want&nbsp;
it I think that there's so much cynicism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:26.960
in the entertainment world and Christmas is about&nbsp;
loving your fellow man, loving your neighbor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:34.240
and unity that I wonder if Hollywood is even&nbsp;
capable of making that type of film? I really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:40.560
wonder that? So look, do I want to see the sequel&nbsp;
to A Christmas story starring Peter Billingsley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:45.920
as a grown-up version of himself, maybe it's&nbsp;
set in the 60’s? I would love to see that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:52.160
Is that going to happen? I don't know. Is it&nbsp;
going to happen to a satisfying degree, we'll see?

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:55.840
Film Courage: Maybe he wants a&nbsp;
glue gun? Maybe he's a crafter?

00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:02.800
Chris: Yeah we'll see but I don't need several&nbsp;
glue guns. So someone who makes props and sets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:10.160
and things but not everybody celebrates Christmas&nbsp;
that's true so so it does alienate many people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:16.240
right different you know whatever and in whatever&nbsp;
it might just be non-religious maybe they don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:23.200
believe in consumerism and things like that there&nbsp;
could be a whole anti-corporate angle to it yeah I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:28.960
mean Black Friday yeah I mean there have been yeah&nbsp;
there have been movies that have explored the over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:35.840
commercialization of Christmas that's fine I think&nbsp;
that's part of it I think that's a valid critique&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:44.160
of the holiday and having said that I love the&nbsp;
decorations I love the excuse to get together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:51.840
with friends and family I love the idea of we're&nbsp;
going to take stock and inventory of the last year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:57.280
and commit to being say a better person in the&nbsp;
new year maybe there have been lessons learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:05.360
and it's that that holiday period where we can&nbsp;
kind of take a step back and assess you know what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:11.600
have you what have we accomplished what are we&nbsp;
capable of doing how can we do better and and how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:19.840
can we contribute to a better world I think that&nbsp;
that that idea that message defies the holiday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:28.080
forget the holiday forget the commercialization&nbsp;
that idea of self-reflection that I think is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:34.400
important for anybody you know no matter whether&nbsp;
you like celebrate the holiday or like it or hate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:42.480
it it doesn't matter that idea is something I&nbsp;
think that we need to do on an annual basis.

